                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fbe3418-d861-3df6-a624-a83f766cb3c8",
                                        "entry_id": "66627c69-4a06-3882-b49d-4c3bd0458656",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To deliberately not listen or pay attention to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "583584ee-adf0-4def-899a-951aa0514e33",
                                                "sense_id": "6fbe3418-d861-3df6-a624-a83f766cb3c8",
                                                "text": "A problem ignored is a problem doubled."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fd3a010-5720-4108-afdd-c52d861ca7fb",
                                                "sense_id": "6fbe3418-d861-3df6-a624-a83f766cb3c8",
                                                "text": "Ignore these four words."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbbf5923-ff49-4361-9687-710f26292738",
                                                "sense_id": "6fbe3418-d861-3df6-a624-a83f766cb3c8",
                                                "text": "One particularly damaging, but often ignored, effect of conflict on education is the proliferation of attacks on schools[…]as children, teachers or school buildings become the targets of attacks. Parents fear sending their children to school. Girls are particularly vulnerable to sexual violence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "747a3cfc-a72e-4069-bbe7-c029a178c127",
                                                "sense_id": "6fbe3418-d861-3df6-a624-a83f766cb3c8",
                                                "text": "The late Professor Pat White was an outspoken critic. In his 1986 book Forgotten Railways, he dismissed as smoke and mirrors the oft-used argument that 33% of rail routes carried only 1% of the traffic, as it ignores the fact that a third of the national road network also only carried 2% of cars and lorries. But unlike rail, road got away with it because no mention was made of how much it cost the taxpayer to keep them usable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a79378d8-eb77-3552-9dee-7f677d130e3d",
                                        "entry_id": "66627c69-4a06-3882-b49d-4c3bd0458656",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To pretend to not notice someone or something."
